{"url": "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/ace/about-us/ace-at-a-glance", "final_url": "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/ace/about-us/ace-at-a-glance", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-18", "text": "Home\nAbout Us\nProgrammes & Admissions\nResearch Clusters\nNews & Events\nPeople\nResources\nAlumni\nQuick Links\nAbout Us\nACE at a Glance\nHome About Us ACE at a Glance\nAbout the Department\nThe Department is unique in Hong Kong and perhaps world-wide for its multidisciplinary faculty that includes specialists in civil and structural engineering, architecture, surveying, building services engineering, construction engineering and management, urban design and regional planning all within one academic unit.\nOur academic offerings are professional-discipline specific through the Discovery-enriched Curriculum, our programmes aim to enhance innovation and exploration of new ideas. Our graduates are well equipped with necessary skills and knowledge to contribute towards a better development of the built environment. Building on these, we offer taught postgraduate master programmes in Civil and Architectural Engineering, Construction Management and Urban Design and Regional Planning. Our graduate research degree programmes include more than 100 MPhil and PhD students.\nThe consultancy activities of the department cover full range of areas in Built Environment. Some recent studies include Civil and Environmental Engineering, Structure and Geotechnical Engineering, Transportation, Hydrology, Building Services Engineering, Construction Management, Surveying, Architecture, Urban Design and Planning. The teaching and research activities of the department are supported by excellent laboratories.\nOur Motto\nMeeting the World\u2019s Challenges: Build Tomorrow, Create the Future\nACE Academic Rankings\n#54\nWorldwide, Civil and Structural Engineering\nQS World University Rankings by Subject 2025\n#55\nWorldwide, Architecture and Built Environment\nQS World University Rankin